WEBVTT

00:00:36.954 --> 00:00:39.039
Push, Mrs. Fry. You're almost there.

00:00:39.122 --> 00:00:41.959
You can do it, honey.
Squeeze one out for America.

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:45.003
Hey, keep it down! It's the ninth inning!

00:00:45.087 --> 00:00:47.172
Here's the 0-2 pitch to Claypool.

00:00:47.256 --> 00:00:50.676
He's taking all the way
for a called strike three.

00:00:50.759 --> 00:00:52.344
Swing the bat, you bum!

00:00:55.138 --> 00:00:57.224
It's a boy. And look at that red hair!

00:00:57.307 --> 00:00:59.226
You saying my son is a commie?

00:00:59.309 --> 00:01:01.603
And Grody leans into the pitch.

00:01:01.687 --> 00:01:04.022
It hits him! The Mets win!

00:01:04.147 --> 00:01:07.359
This is the happiest day of my life!

00:01:07.442 --> 00:01:08.527
Here's your baby, ma'am.

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:09.736
Yeah, okay, thanks.

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:11.864
So, what should we name him?

00:01:11.947 --> 00:01:13.866
Eh, you pick. I picked dinner last night.

00:01:13.949 --> 00:01:17.452
Well, I was thinking of Philip,
after those screwdrivers.

00:01:17.536 --> 00:01:19.246
That's a fantastic idea.

00:01:19.329 --> 00:01:20.998
More morphine, please.

00:01:22.374 --> 00:01:24.793
Look, Yancy, it's
your baby brother Philip.

00:01:24.877 --> 00:01:27.004
I wanna be named Philip!

00:01:27.087 --> 00:01:29.339
Me Philip! Me Philip!

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:31.758
Son, your name is Yancy,

00:01:31.842 --> 00:01:34.928
just like me and my grandfather,
and so on,

00:01:35.012 --> 00:01:38.765
all the way back to minuteman Yancy Fry,

00:01:38.849 --> 00:01:42.060
who blasted commies
in the American Revolution.

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:47.691
Philip, until I find
a suitable model of an ICBM,

00:01:47.774 --> 00:01:51.236
you'll have to make do
learning to fear this toy spacecraft.

00:01:56.158 --> 00:01:58.452
Mine! Mine!

00:02:19.306 --> 00:02:20.307
Come on!

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:22.017
Baby needs a new pair of shoes!

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:25.020
To hell with your spoiled baby.
I need those shoes!

00:02:28.148 --> 00:02:29.983
And it's a dead heat!

00:02:30.067 --> 00:02:32.569
They're checking the electron microscope.

00:02:32.653 --> 00:02:34.238
And the winner is

00:02:34.696 --> 00:02:37.824
number three in a quantum finish!

00:02:37.908 --> 00:02:38.992
No fair!

00:02:39.076 --> 00:02:41.453
You changed the outcome by measuring it!

00:02:42.329 --> 00:02:43.455
How'd you do, Fry?

00:02:43.539 --> 00:02:45.415
I'll tell you when my horse finishes.

00:02:46.667 --> 00:02:47.668
Bad.

00:02:49.753 --> 00:02:52.464
In today's field,
we own four horses and two jockeys.

00:02:52.548 --> 00:02:54.967
We just put our best jockey
out to stud, Amy.

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:56.426
He's perfect for you.

00:02:57.302 --> 00:02:59.930
Hey, baby, ever do it in a suitcase?

00:03:00.013 --> 00:03:02.432
Ooh, look! It's the centaur race!

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:05.978
Ow! Oh!

00:03:07.771 --> 00:03:09.690
Come on, come on!

00:03:09.773 --> 00:03:11.859
Hey, Leela, how about a kiss
for good luck?

00:03:14.069 --> 00:03:15.487
I meant tongue luck.

00:03:15.696 --> 00:03:16.864
Ow! Ow!

00:03:16.947 --> 00:03:20.742
And the winner is
number four, Steven!

00:03:20.868 --> 00:03:23.078
I am so unlucky.

00:03:23.161 --> 00:03:25.831
I've run over black cats
that were luckier than me.

00:03:26.123 --> 00:03:30.335
Get your piping hot horse burgers,
horse fries, horse cakes and shakes.

00:03:30.419 --> 00:03:32.880
We got tongue
straight from the horse's mouth.

00:03:33.088 --> 00:03:34.631
- Hmm...
- It all sounds good.

00:03:34.715 --> 00:03:37.259
All our horses are 100% horse-fed

00:03:37.342 --> 00:03:39.720
for that double-horse, juiced-in goodness.

00:03:39.803 --> 00:03:43.348
I'll have the cholesterol-free omelet
with Horse Beaters.

00:03:43.432 --> 00:03:45.726
And you, sir? How can I horse you?

00:03:45.809 --> 00:03:47.060
I'll have a horse Coke.

00:03:47.144 --> 00:03:48.395
Horse Pepsi okay?

00:03:48.478 --> 00:03:49.479
Nay.

00:04:08.665 --> 00:04:09.958
Hey, what are you doing?

00:04:10.042 --> 00:04:11.043
This.

00:04:13.712 --> 00:04:15.047
Dear horse god,

00:04:15.130 --> 00:04:16.882
I know I don't usually pray to you.

00:04:16.965 --> 00:04:18.717
Sometimes I doubt you even exist.

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:22.596
But if you're willing to grant me luck,
please stamp your hoof once.

00:04:28.894 --> 00:04:30.437
Come on, number six! Move it!

00:04:34.316 --> 00:04:35.943
Don't do that! What are you...

00:04:37.694 --> 00:04:38.904
Man, it's contagious.

00:04:39.488 --> 00:04:41.782
And the winner is Harry Trotter

00:04:41.865 --> 00:04:44.034
by the entire racetrack.

00:04:45.369 --> 00:04:46.703
Yahoo!

00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:49.790
That'll teach those other horses
to take drugs.

00:04:50.749 --> 00:04:52.084
That's it!

00:04:52.167 --> 00:04:55.921
You can only take my money
for so long before you take it all,

00:04:56.004 --> 00:04:57.339
and I say enough!

00:04:57.798 --> 00:04:59.508
I've got $1 left,

00:04:59.591 --> 00:05:01.385
and this one I'm holding on to.

00:05:02.678 --> 00:05:03.971
Oh, no, you don't.

00:05:14.273 --> 00:05:15.983
I may not know much about horses,

00:05:16.066 --> 00:05:19.319
but I know a lot
about doing anything for $1.

00:05:24.616 --> 00:05:26.535
If you think bad luck can defeat me,

00:05:26.618 --> 00:05:29.913
then you don't know my name is Philip J...

00:05:32.457 --> 00:05:33.458
Phew!

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:41.842
That is one unlucky guy.

00:05:49.641 --> 00:05:51.185
Kareem's got the skyhook,

00:05:51.268 --> 00:05:54.021
but Philip J. Fry's got the space-hook.

00:05:58.525 --> 00:05:59.735
Yancy drives.

00:05:59.818 --> 00:06:01.987
He goes up with his patented space-hook.

00:06:03.071 --> 00:06:05.574
Hey! That's my patented space-hook.

00:06:05.657 --> 00:06:06.825
You stole it.

00:06:06.909 --> 00:06:08.493
You're not the president of it.

00:06:16.668 --> 00:06:18.170
Holy camoly!

00:06:18.253 --> 00:06:19.755
A seven-leaf clover!

00:06:19.838 --> 00:06:21.798
I'm dying of old age!

00:06:32.601 --> 00:06:34.895
Game over! Phil wins!

00:06:34.978 --> 00:06:37.105
Yancy's fans are stunned!

00:06:37.189 --> 00:06:40.317
There'll be no celebration
at the Yancydome!

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:41.527
Lucky.

00:06:50.702 --> 00:06:52.704
Well, someone's in a good mode.

00:06:52.788 --> 00:06:55.415
Let's just say I lucked out at the track.

00:06:55.499 --> 00:06:56.917
Also, I rigged one race.

00:06:57.084 --> 00:06:59.169
I'd have won
a lot of money, too,

00:06:59.253 --> 00:07:01.630
if I still had my lucky seven-leaf clover.

00:07:01.713 --> 00:07:03.298
Plus, I'd still have my hair.

00:07:04.591 --> 00:07:05.968
I got your page, Mr. Fry.

00:07:06.051 --> 00:07:07.094
Your new hair is ready.

00:07:09.888 --> 00:07:11.932
So, whatever happened
to this seven-leaf clover?

00:07:12.015 --> 00:07:15.143
I hid it in a secret hiding place
whose location I never told anyone.

00:07:15.227 --> 00:07:16.436
Not even Scruffy.

00:07:19.439 --> 00:07:22.150
So the clover is still
in the hiding place, maybe?

00:07:22.234 --> 00:07:24.486
Hey, yeah, maybe it is still there,

00:07:24.570 --> 00:07:26.822
underground in the ruins of Old New York,

00:07:26.905 --> 00:07:28.740
helping some ant defeat another ant.

00:07:28.824 --> 00:07:30.993
Or helping some piece of dirt
turn its luck around.

00:07:31.076 --> 00:07:32.786
Dirt doesn't need luck.

00:07:32.870 --> 00:07:35.455
I'm going down there
to get my clover back.

00:07:35.998 --> 00:07:37.583
Some of the tunnels have metal bars,

00:07:37.666 --> 00:07:39.751
so I'll need someone
who's good at bending.

00:07:39.835 --> 00:07:41.670
- Leela, how about you?
- Sure, I'll do it.

00:07:41.753 --> 00:07:42.921
Like hell you will!

00:07:43.005 --> 00:07:44.298
Bending is my middle name.

00:07:44.381 --> 00:07:45.549
- It is?
- Yeah.

00:07:45.632 --> 00:07:49.261
My full name is Bender Bending Rodriguez.

00:07:51.722 --> 00:07:52.723
Here's the entrance.

00:07:52.806 --> 00:07:54.183
From this moment on,

00:07:54.266 --> 00:07:57.269
I declare my bad luck officially over.

00:08:01.481 --> 00:08:02.608
He was fun.

00:08:09.031 --> 00:08:11.033
Well, if we get bored
looking for the clover,

00:08:11.116 --> 00:08:12.701
I've got Tetris on this thing.

00:08:14.328 --> 00:08:15.746
Look, up ahead.

00:08:15.829 --> 00:08:17.331
Old New York.

00:08:17.414 --> 00:08:20.792
The city that inspired
a casino in Las Vegas.

00:08:21.877 --> 00:08:24.213
Wow, we've got Manhattan all to ourselves.

00:08:24.296 --> 00:08:27.925
I can finally do all the crazy stuff
I always dreamed of doing.

00:08:28.759 --> 00:08:30.761
Howard Stern is overrated!

00:08:33.430 --> 00:08:35.057
Oh... Oops!

00:08:35.265 --> 00:08:37.017
New York is so burned!

00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:39.811
Remember when Mayor Giuliani
cracked down on jaywalking?

00:08:39.895 --> 00:08:42.898
- No.
- Well, Rudy, how do you like this action?

00:08:43.065 --> 00:08:44.066
Ooh!

00:08:51.323 --> 00:08:54.201
As you know,
the big break-dance battle is Saturday.

00:08:54.284 --> 00:08:55.285
So if we want to win

00:08:55.369 --> 00:08:57.829
those Jam Master Jay
autographed parachute pants,

00:08:57.913 --> 00:08:59.498
our crew has to pop,

00:08:59.581 --> 00:09:01.917
lock and bust the freshest.

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:04.753
Noticeably F.A.T., drop us a beat.

00:09:08.757 --> 00:09:10.592
- Name?
- Cosmic F.

00:09:11.134 --> 00:09:12.970
- Style?
- Outer space.

00:09:13.053 --> 00:09:14.304
Special moves?

00:09:14.388 --> 00:09:15.389
The moonwalk.

00:09:16.139 --> 00:09:17.140
The robot.

00:09:17.933 --> 00:09:19.351
The Zero G.

00:09:21.311 --> 00:09:23.355
- Name?
- Cosmic Y.

00:09:23.438 --> 00:09:24.439
Style?

00:09:24.565 --> 00:09:26.066
Uh... Deep space.

00:09:26.149 --> 00:09:27.568
"Deep space"?

00:09:27.651 --> 00:09:28.777
Special moves?

00:09:28.861 --> 00:09:30.445
- The space walk.
- Hey!

00:09:30.529 --> 00:09:33.574
- The robot.
- The robot? That's similar to mine!

00:09:33.657 --> 00:09:35.033
The Zero G.

00:09:37.369 --> 00:09:40.080
What are you doing?
You totally ripped off my routine.

00:09:40.163 --> 00:09:41.498
You calling me a biter?

00:09:42.791 --> 00:09:46.003
Why do you always have to steal
everything from me, Yancy?

00:09:46.086 --> 00:09:47.713
Find your own life and live it.

00:09:47.796 --> 00:09:49.715
Stop illin'. Word.

00:09:49.798 --> 00:09:51.925
Well, I'd like to see you
try to steal this!

00:09:52.009 --> 00:09:53.886
The septuple head spin.

00:09:54.011 --> 00:09:56.471
He's just scratching.

00:09:56.555 --> 00:09:58.682
No one's ever done more than a quadruple.

00:09:58.765 --> 00:09:59.766
Oh, yeah?

00:09:59.850 --> 00:10:02.352
Noticeably F.A.T., rewind the tape.

00:10:18.327 --> 00:10:19.786
Crazy sucker.

00:10:21.538 --> 00:10:23.415
Phil, you're hype!

00:10:23.498 --> 00:10:25.334
That was ice-cold, bro.

00:10:25.417 --> 00:10:29.296
Fry, if I ever see you try
anything that crazy again,

00:10:29.755 --> 00:10:33.717
this crew might just have
some new parachute pants!

00:10:37.930 --> 00:10:39.806
Stop hogging the clover!

00:10:42.142 --> 00:10:43.143
Ow!

00:10:52.903 --> 00:10:55.822
All right, team.
Let's go find that clover.

00:10:55.906 --> 00:10:57.074
Which way to your house?

00:10:57.157 --> 00:10:59.034
The sign says we're at 71st Street.

00:10:59.117 --> 00:11:00.827
71st Street?

00:11:00.953 --> 00:11:02.621
Hmm. Never heard of it.

00:11:02.704 --> 00:11:04.623
Downtown could be in any direction.

00:11:04.706 --> 00:11:05.707
No sweat.

00:11:05.791 --> 00:11:08.126
We'll just take a spin on the B train.

00:11:08.627 --> 00:11:09.920
Ooh!

00:11:10.003 --> 00:11:11.755
That feels funny.

00:11:14.174 --> 00:11:16.009
This is
the Brooklyn-bound B train,

00:11:16.093 --> 00:11:18.637
making local stops
at wherever the hell I feel like.

00:11:18.720 --> 00:11:20.222
Watch for the closing doors.

00:11:36.280 --> 00:11:38.115
Wake up, buddy. End of the line.

00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:43.787
Gosh, my old neighborhood.

00:11:43.954 --> 00:11:44.955
Oh!

00:11:45.038 --> 00:11:47.207
That's the bench
where I found some shirts!

00:11:47.291 --> 00:11:50.210
That fire hydrant,
in the summer, we'd light on fire.

00:11:50.711 --> 00:11:52.921
On that corner,
some guy with a bushy beard

00:11:53.005 --> 00:11:54.756
handed out a socialist newsletter.

00:11:54.840 --> 00:11:56.175
Was it poorly xeroxed?

00:11:56.258 --> 00:11:57.426
You better believe it.

00:11:57.509 --> 00:11:59.219
The old comedians were right.

00:11:59.303 --> 00:12:01.263
This place is a lot different from LA.

00:12:02.264 --> 00:12:05.601
Pardon me. Did I overhear you say
you used to live here?

00:12:05.684 --> 00:12:08.103
- That's right.
- Did you know Andy Goldman?

00:12:08.187 --> 00:12:10.272
Yeah. He was my neighbor. Why?

00:12:10.355 --> 00:12:12.065
I mutated from him!

00:12:12.149 --> 00:12:13.442
Get outta here!

00:12:13.525 --> 00:12:15.194
What's Andy up to these days?

00:12:16.195 --> 00:12:18.113
The short answer is, I'm teaching.

00:12:18.697 --> 00:12:20.949
- He seemed nice.
- Sure, when he's sober.

00:12:24.328 --> 00:12:25.579
Holy camoly!

00:12:25.662 --> 00:12:26.997
The house I grew up in!

00:12:27.080 --> 00:12:28.248
It's still there!

00:12:29.291 --> 00:12:32.336
Man, Father Time
really took a bat to this place.

00:12:35.756 --> 00:12:39.468
That stupid clover
is a worthless piece of garbage!

00:12:39.551 --> 00:12:40.677
Give it, give it, give it!

00:12:40.761 --> 00:12:42.262
Mom! Help!

00:12:43.889 --> 00:12:44.890
Yes!

00:12:44.973 --> 00:12:47.184
Mom, Yancy's trying to steal my clover.

00:12:47.267 --> 00:12:49.353
Yancy, stealing is wrong.

00:12:50.354 --> 00:12:51.855
- I'm gonna pile-drive you!
- Stop it!

00:12:51.939 --> 00:12:53.190
You're dead meat!

00:12:55.484 --> 00:12:56.944
What's happening up there?

00:12:57.027 --> 00:12:59.321
Did Kremlin Joe let fly with the nukes?

00:12:59.404 --> 00:13:00.531
Not yet, Commander.

00:13:00.614 --> 00:13:03.325
Yancy's just trying
to steal my stuff, as usual.

00:13:03.408 --> 00:13:06.036
Well, he'd better keep
his hands off these bananas.

00:13:06.453 --> 00:13:09.456
Gonna need them when the radiation
turns us all into monkeys.

00:13:13.460 --> 00:13:15.170
The Ronco Record Vault.

00:13:15.254 --> 00:13:18.757
Yancy will never get his hands on you
in here, or my money back.

00:13:21.426 --> 00:13:23.971
Ah! The Breakfast Club soundtrack.

00:13:24.054 --> 00:13:27.474
Man, I can't wait till I'm old enough
to feel ways about stuff.

00:13:31.854 --> 00:13:33.146
Stay safe, clover.

00:13:33.230 --> 00:13:34.940
I may need you again someday.

00:13:45.242 --> 00:13:46.493
This was the storage room.

00:13:46.577 --> 00:13:49.288
My dad spent years
turning it into a bomb shelter.

00:13:49.371 --> 00:13:52.499
And yet you guys never had
a single nuclear war.

00:13:52.583 --> 00:13:53.750
What a waste.

00:13:54.126 --> 00:13:55.210
This is it.

00:13:55.294 --> 00:13:57.171
My Ronco Record Vault.

00:13:58.755 --> 00:14:00.549
I still remember the combination.

00:14:02.050 --> 00:14:03.051
Three.

00:14:04.720 --> 00:14:05.721
It's stuck.

00:14:05.804 --> 00:14:10.517
The Achilles' heel of the Ronco design
is its structural resonance frequency.

00:14:10.601 --> 00:14:11.685
Allow me.

00:14:21.778 --> 00:14:23.030
There we go.

00:14:24.489 --> 00:14:25.490
Here it is.

00:14:25.574 --> 00:14:27.326
The Breakfast Club soundtrack.

00:14:27.409 --> 00:14:29.453
You mean breakfast club sandwich.

00:14:29.536 --> 00:14:32.372
I hid my seven-leaf clover
in this very record jacket,

00:14:32.456 --> 00:14:34.166
so my brother Yancy wouldn't get it.

00:14:35.292 --> 00:14:36.293
Here goes.

00:14:37.336 --> 00:14:38.337
It's gone!

00:14:39.630 --> 00:14:41.924
The whole place has been cleaned out!

00:14:42.007 --> 00:14:44.718
Yancy stole my clover. That thief!

00:14:44.801 --> 00:14:46.595
How do you know it didn't disintegrate?

00:14:46.678 --> 00:14:48.680
Everything else in here held up okay.

00:14:48.764 --> 00:14:50.891
Except Sports by Huey Lewis.

00:14:54.478 --> 00:14:57.064
I don't know why my brother
hated me so much.

00:14:57.272 --> 00:14:59.358
Oh... Brothers always fight.

00:14:59.441 --> 00:15:01.443
I'm sure deep down he loved you.

00:15:01.527 --> 00:15:04.613
He just never got a chance to say it
before you got frozen.

00:15:04.696 --> 00:15:05.781
You think?

00:15:05.864 --> 00:15:07.366
'Cause I always kind of wished that...

00:15:09.284 --> 00:15:11.286
Who is that godlike figure?

00:15:11.370 --> 00:15:12.955
It's my brother, Yancy!

00:15:13.038 --> 00:15:16.458
And there, in his lapel,
my seven-leaf clover!

00:15:16.542 --> 00:15:17.918
I knew he stole it!

00:15:18.001 --> 00:15:19.002
Hold the phone.

00:15:19.086 --> 00:15:22.589
If that's Yancy, why does
the inscription say "Philip J. Fry"?

00:15:22.756 --> 00:15:25.175
Wait a second. That's my name.

00:15:25.259 --> 00:15:26.260
Good Lord!

00:15:26.343 --> 00:15:28.971
He ditched his goofy name and stole mine!

00:15:29.054 --> 00:15:31.348
Apparently, this brave Adonis,

00:15:31.431 --> 00:15:33.475
this Cadillac of men,

00:15:33.559 --> 00:15:35.978
was the "first person on Mars."

00:15:36.061 --> 00:15:37.271
First person on Mars?

00:15:37.354 --> 00:15:39.773
I should have been
the first person on Mars!

00:15:39.857 --> 00:15:41.149
He stole my clover,

00:15:41.233 --> 00:15:43.443
he stole my name, and he stole my life.

00:15:44.945 --> 00:15:46.613
And now he broke my hand.

00:15:46.697 --> 00:15:48.991
His legend lives on.

00:15:53.662 --> 00:15:56.582
So you opened the record vault,
and the clover was gone?

00:15:56.665 --> 00:16:00.294
Yep. Nothing in there
but all the best music of the 1980s

00:16:00.377 --> 00:16:01.837
in one amazing collection.

00:16:01.920 --> 00:16:04.798
Survivor, Pat Benatar, the Scorpions.

00:16:04.882 --> 00:16:05.924
The list goes on.

00:16:06.008 --> 00:16:09.845
That clover helped my rat fink brother
steal my dream of going into space.

00:16:09.928 --> 00:16:11.388
Now I'll never get there.

00:16:11.471 --> 00:16:13.473
You went there this morning for doughnuts.

00:16:13.557 --> 00:16:15.601
"First person on Mars."

00:16:15.684 --> 00:16:18.187
Oh! So your brother
was that Philip J. Fry.

00:16:18.312 --> 00:16:20.314
I'm Philip J. Fry!

00:16:20.397 --> 00:16:22.482
He stole my name after I got frozen.

00:16:22.566 --> 00:16:23.859
Shut up, friends.

00:16:23.942 --> 00:16:27.112
My Internet browser
heard us saying the word "Fry,"

00:16:27.196 --> 00:16:30.532
and it found a movie
about Philip J. Fry for us.

00:16:31.491 --> 00:16:34.203
It also opened my calendar to Friday

00:16:34.286 --> 00:16:36.079
and ordered me some French fries.

00:16:39.291 --> 00:16:40.709
Philip J. Fry,

00:16:40.792 --> 00:16:43.170
astronaut, philanthropist, entrepreneur,

00:16:43.253 --> 00:16:46.173
was a great man truly worthy of narration.

00:16:46.673 --> 00:16:48.634
Fry was the first man on Mars,

00:16:48.717 --> 00:16:50.761
a feat that has never since been equaled.

00:16:50.844 --> 00:16:52.304
That should've been me!

00:16:52.387 --> 00:16:54.056
The ever-lucky Fry

00:16:54.139 --> 00:16:56.183
made his fortune after striking oil

00:16:56.266 --> 00:16:59.144
in the bathroom of the mansion
he had won in a lottery.

00:16:59.645 --> 00:17:01.897
That's my clover! Yancy stole it.

00:17:01.980 --> 00:17:05.400
After a whirlwind fling
with Icelandic supermodel Njord,

00:17:05.484 --> 00:17:07.361
Fry scored a string of top-10 hits

00:17:07.444 --> 00:17:09.029
with his rock band Leaf Seven,

00:17:09.112 --> 00:17:10.697
known for their hypnotic rhythms,

00:17:10.781 --> 00:17:12.908
driving bass lines and memorable hooks.

00:17:12.991 --> 00:17:14.409
That's what I'm known for!

00:17:14.493 --> 00:17:15.953
Phil came in, right?

00:17:16.036 --> 00:17:18.080
He strummed out this tune, yeah?

00:17:18.163 --> 00:17:20.249
And I said, "That's a number-one record."

00:17:20.332 --> 00:17:23.043
Today,
Fry spends most of his time

00:17:23.126 --> 00:17:26.171
in his grave
at Orbiting Meadows National Cemetery,

00:17:26.255 --> 00:17:28.590
buried with the trademark
seven-leaf clover

00:17:28.674 --> 00:17:30.425
that will bring him luck in the next life,

00:17:30.509 --> 00:17:32.261
perhaps, some Egyptians believe.

00:17:32.344 --> 00:17:34.137
So that's where my clover is.

00:17:34.221 --> 00:17:36.598
Hey, is that orbiting cemetery near here?

00:17:36.682 --> 00:17:38.475
It will be in a couple hours.

00:17:38.559 --> 00:17:40.727
Good. Leela, Bender,

00:17:40.811 --> 00:17:42.354
we're going grave robbing.

00:17:42.437 --> 00:17:43.605
I'll get my kit!

00:17:48.360 --> 00:17:49.945
Thanks for lending me your tux, Dad.

00:17:50.028 --> 00:17:51.488
It'll be perfect for my wedding.

00:17:51.989 --> 00:17:55.576
Yancy, that tux got me
through 'Nam in style.

00:17:57.244 --> 00:17:59.913
I just wish your brother
was still around to see this.

00:17:59.997 --> 00:18:02.374
I'll never forget the day
Philip disappeared.

00:18:02.457 --> 00:18:04.668
Wisconsin won the Rose Bowl, 17-9.

00:18:04.751 --> 00:18:06.336
Oh, I miss him.

00:18:06.628 --> 00:18:09.798
Ooh, that reminds me. I was thinking
I'd rummage through Phil's records

00:18:09.882 --> 00:18:12.551
- for something to play at the wedding.
- Have a look downstairs.

00:18:12.634 --> 00:18:14.845
Your brother may be missing,
but his crap sure isn't.

00:18:43.790 --> 00:18:45.334
Huh. Breakfast Club.

00:18:45.417 --> 00:18:48.170
This'll clear out the room
at the end of the reception.

00:19:02.184 --> 00:19:04.895
They buried your brother
in the "World Heroes" section?

00:19:04.978 --> 00:19:06.021
I'm impressed.

00:19:06.104 --> 00:19:07.898
I should be the one in that grave!

00:19:21.995 --> 00:19:23.872
Hmm. We lost Bender.

00:19:24.373 --> 00:19:25.374
There.

00:19:25.457 --> 00:19:29.628
Now no one will be able to say
I don't own John Larroquette's spine.

00:19:31.922 --> 00:19:33.966
Aha! My brother's grave.

00:19:40.097 --> 00:19:42.224
Oh, it's all lies, every word of it.

00:19:42.307 --> 00:19:44.393
He wasn't original. He wasn't a Martian.

00:19:44.476 --> 00:19:45.686
He wasn't Philip Fry.

00:19:45.769 --> 00:19:47.604
And since when is he a "The"?

00:19:47.688 --> 00:19:50.148
You're twice the "The" he ever was.

00:19:50.232 --> 00:19:52.067
It's clovering time.

00:20:08.083 --> 00:20:10.502
So, had any ideas for names, Yancy?

00:20:10.711 --> 00:20:12.963
Mmm, I'm sort of thinking of one.

00:20:13.755 --> 00:20:16.091
Daddy has a present for you today.

00:20:16.175 --> 00:20:17.217
Do you know what it is?

00:20:17.676 --> 00:20:21.221
It's a lucky clover that can help you
be successful, whatever you do.

00:20:21.305 --> 00:20:22.514
Even break dancing.

00:20:22.598 --> 00:20:25.142
And it once belonged
to someone very special.

00:20:25.809 --> 00:20:27.936
I know what name
you want to give him, Yancy.

00:20:28.020 --> 00:20:29.605
- It's okay.
- Really?

00:20:30.647 --> 00:20:31.648
Son,

00:20:31.732 --> 00:20:34.109
I'm naming you Philip J. Fry,

00:20:34.193 --> 00:20:35.903
in honor of my little brother,

00:20:36.486 --> 00:20:38.030
who I miss every day.

00:20:39.198 --> 00:20:40.282
I love you, Philip,

00:20:41.617 --> 00:20:42.784
and I always will.

00:21:02.429 --> 00:21:06.350
Pay dirt! I got the clover,
plus his wedding ring.

00:21:06.433 --> 00:21:08.101
Sorry, ladies, I'm taken.

00:21:08.644 --> 00:21:11.313
Hey, Fry, you want me
to smack the corpse up a little?

00:21:19.488 --> 00:21:22.741
Uh, Bender,
I think Fry needs a moment alone.

00:21:22.824 --> 00:21:24.409
All right. Grab a shovel.

00:21:24.493 --> 00:21:27.204
I'm only one skull short
of a Mouseketeer reunion.

00:21:29.706 --> 00:21:31.208
Don't you

00:21:32.167 --> 00:21:34.086
Forget about me

00:21:35.754 --> 00:21:38.173
Don't, don't, don't, don't

00:21:38.382 --> 00:21:40.259
Don't you

00:21:40.801 --> 00:21:42.761
Forget about me

00:21:46.557 --> 00:21:50.435
Will you recognize me

00:21:50.769 --> 00:21:54.815
Call my name or walk on by